Exercise: sa-selinux-review (chapter 16 lab)

Work on servera, with sudo or as root. SELinux must stay in enforcing mode
the whole time.

The portal
 1. Install httpd (and audit, setroubleshoot-server for diagnosis), start
    auditd, and enable and start httpd.
 2. Serve /srv/portal (index.html containing the text "Portal is up") on
    TCP port 8090 only: set "Listen 8090" instead of "Listen 80" in
    /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf, and a DocumentRoot of /srv/portal with
    "Require all granted" in a file under /etc/httpd/conf.d/.
 3. Make it work with SELinux enforcing:
      - label the port 8090 for web servers,
      - add a permanent file-context rule for /srv/portal and everything
        below it, and apply it,
      - turn on the boolean httpd_can_network_connect permanently (the
        portal will later talk to a back-end),
      - leave httpd_enable_homedirs off.
    Test with: curl http://localhost:8090/

On workstation
 4. Fill in answers.txt.

Then, on workstation:  lab grade sa-selinux-review
